      "problem": "Find $p$ if $-2$ is a root of $f(x)=3p{x}^{2}-21px-18.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since  $x=-2$ is a root, we have $f(-2)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=-2,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p(-2)^{2}-21p(-2)-18 & =0 \\\\ 12p+42p-18 & =0 \\\\ 54p-18 & =0 \\\\ 54p & =18 \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
